70,"dissolved":-255,"enwiki":"Eastern Zhou","summary":"The Eastern Zhou (; c. 770–256 BC) is a period in Chinese history comprising the latter half of the Zhou dynasty, following the Western Zhou era and the royal court's relocation eastward from Fenghao to Chengzhou (near present-day Luoyang). The Eastern Zhou was characterised by the weakened authority of the Ji family, the Zhou royal house. It is subdivided into two parts: the Spring and Autumn period (c. 770 – c. 481 or 476 BC), during which the ancient aristocracy still held power in a large number of separate polities, and the Warring States period (c. 481 or 476 – 221 BC), which saw the consolidation of territory and escalation of interstate warfare and administrative sophistication."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q307066","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q187136","value_label":"Luoyang","from_t":-770,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Luoyang"},{"qid":"Q307066","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q849242","value_label":"hereditary monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"hereditary monarchy"},{"qid":"Q307066","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q7269","value_label":"monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"monarchy"},{"qid":"Q307066","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q1069609","value_label":"Western Zhou","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Western Zhou"},{"qid":"Q307066","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q34756","value_label":"Qin","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Qin"}],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Chou Dynasty","Dinastia Zhou orientale","Dinastía Zhou Oriental","Dong Zhou","Doğu Zhou Hanedanı","Dynastie Zhou de l'Est","Dynastie Zhou orientale","Dynastie des Zhou orientaux","Eastern Chou","Eastern Zhou","Eastern Zhou Dynasty","Eastern Zhou period","Kingdom of Zhou","O